msgid "<code>schedutil</code> raises the clock with the load and saves energy at idle. <code>performance</code> keeps the maximum frequency all the time: measured on this router it needed 28%% less CPU per Gbit/s on Wi-Fi to LAN bridging and lowered the idle Wi-Fi latency by about 0.2 ms, but the throughput and the latency under load stayed the same and the router ran about 2 °C warmer."
